build/
build-*/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.geode
# what leveldp writes when it is run without --out, so it cannot be committed by accident
leveldp_plan.txt*
# data/ is an allow-list. Only the solver's results (solution_lv*_dp.txt), the
# cold regression's baseline and the calibration levels (data/rigs/*.lvl) are
# tracked. Everything the tools
# regenerate per run (.best/.gbest/.dump/.trace/.tail/.fixups/.bands/.groups,
# run logs) is not. The official-level dumps (objrects/triggers/objgroups/obb),
# gdref and the fixups_log archives live outside this repository
# (GDSOLVER_LAB, see py/gdtas/paths.py).
data/*
# The 22 official-level solutions, and only those. A long campaign leaves a
# lineage of intermediate plans behind (solution_lv22rNN, solution_lv22cold*,
# lv16A/B, the first lv22 clear); they are working files, they do NOT replay to
# a clear (verified 2026-08-23: 70 of them FAIL), and publishing them would mean
# handing out 70 files that call themselves solutions and are not.
!data/solution_lv[0-9]_dp.txt
!data/solution_lv1[0-9]_dp.txt
!data/solution_lv2[0-2]_dp.txt
# What py/cold_regress.py compares against: the iteration count each level took
# the last time the suite was green, and the [fp] it ended on. It is the
# acceptance record, so it belongs with the code it judges.
!data/cold_baseline.json
!data/rigs/
data/rigs/*
!data/rigs/*.lvl
!data/rigs/*.units.json
!data/rigs/*.plan.txt
!data/rigs/calib_empty_plan.txt

__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/tmp_quickregress/

# Isolated data roots used for one cold run / A-B comparison (~1.5 GB each)
data-cold*/
data-*/

# Local MCP registration (paths are machine-specific); see .mcp.json.example
.mcp.json
# Private instructions / skills for this machine
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/

# Semantic code index (cocoindex-code); machine-local
/.cocoindex_code/
